            <ArticleTitle>Unusual splenic hemangioma of a pediatric patient: hypointense on T2-weighted image.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>553-555</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0899-7071(14)00053-9</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.clinimag.2014.02.007</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Splenic hemangioma is a very rare neoplasm in children. On magnetic resonance imaging, splenic hemangioma shows high signal intensity on T2-weighted images. In this report, we present the first pediatric case of a splenic hemangioma, which was significantly hypointense on T2-weighted images.</AbstractText>
